# Dotfiles / bootstrap (agent)

Human docs: `README.md`. WSL: `wsl-bootstrap.mdc`.

## Architecture
- Declarative first (`dot_*`, `private_*`, `dot_config/...`); scripts last.
- `run_once_*` / `run_onchange_*`: small, idempotent; packages/migrations only.
- One bootstrap style: `bootstrap.ps1` / `bootstrap.sh` → tool → init/apply|update → optional SSH.
- Ship Linux + Windows unless OS-specific; templates only for real diffs.
- Secrets local (`config.d`, chezmoi config). Migrations backup first (`run_once_*`).
- Profiles soft-fail on missing/mismatched bins — never `eval` broken init.
- Ensure `~/.local/bin` on PATH before relying on user-installed tools.

## Dependencies / ABI
- Pin self-installed bins in `.chezmoidata.toml`; float apt (`zsh`, `fzf`, …).
- Preferred + floor when PPAs lag: `git` + `git_minimum` (≥ 2.35 / `zdiff3`). Ubuntu 20.04 git-core PPA ~2.50 max.
- Pins: `chezmoi`, `oh_my_posh`, `git`, `git_minimum` — bump in data file only.
- New pin: data → installer → soft-fail guard → CI asset check.
- **glibc floor:** Go/CGO release builds from Ubuntu 22.04+ need `GLIBC_2.32`/`2.34`. Ubuntu 20.04 (2.31) fails with `version GLIBC_2.3x not found`. Prefer/detect musl (static) or older-compatible assets; do not assume `*-linux-amd64` / `*-glibc*` runs everywhere.
- Chezmoi amd64: musl on musl hosts **or** when host glibc < 2.32; else `linux-glibc`. Verify `--version` after extract; retry musl on linker errors.
- Downloads: winget/apt when exact; else GitHub → `$HOME/.cache/...`, retry, checksum, `~/.local/bin`. No bare `curl | sh` for critical bins on flaky nets.
- Re-runnable: skip if desired version already present.

## Validation / debug
- `bash ./scripts/ci-check.sh`. CI: shellcheck, chezmoi dry-run, templates, pin URLs, PS parse.
- Outer “bootstrap failed” = child exit only — `bash -x` / PS trace in-target.

